<!--sheet-->
# Design states of a steel beam

A beam passes through a fixed set of checks before it is issued. The state diagram shows the
order and the way back when a check fails. The checks under it are the same steps, so the state
this beam reaches can be read from the results.

```mermaid
stateDiagram-v2
  [*] --> Sized: section chosen
  Sized --> Bending: check M*
  Bending --> Shear: M* <= phi Ms
  Bending --> Sized: fails, resize
  Shear --> Deflection: V* <= phi Vv
  Shear --> Sized: fails, resize
  Deflection --> Issued: deflection <= L/250
  Deflection --> Sized: fails, resize
  Issued --> [*]
```

## Inputs
L: 7.2 m | span
w: 9.5 kN/m | design load for strength
w_s: 6 kN/m | load for deflection
fy: 300 MPa | yield strength
E: 200000 MPa | elastic modulus
Ze: 775000 mm³ | effective section modulus
I: 121000000 mm⁴ | second moment of area
A_w: 2430 mm² | web area

## Bending
Mstar: w * L^2 / 8 -> kN*m | design moment
phiMs: 0.9 * fy * Ze -> kN*m | design capacity

## Shear
Vstar: w * L / 2 -> kN | design shear
phiVv: 0.9 * 0.6 * fy * A_w -> kN | web shear capacity

## Deflection
delta: 5 * w_s * L^4 / (384 * E * I) -> mm | midspan deflection
delta_lim: L / 250 -> mm | limit

if Mstar <= phiMs and Vstar <= phiVv and delta <= delta_lim: "State reached: Issued." else: "State reached: back to Sized."
